## Hard stops (reject before ship)

**Surface discipline**
- Applying Conversion intensity (strong anatomy, emotional composition, competing filled CTAs) to a Receipt/Settings surface → **reject.**
- More than one filled primary CTA dominating a surface → **reject.**
- Filled primary on a Receipt/Settings surface where the action isn't genuinely dominant → **reject** (use `.btn-ghost` / text).

**Type**
- An **operational** number, coordinate, value, metric, receipt date, input, or standalone count rendered in serif/Jost → **reject.** (Numbers *inside natural Jost sentences* are fine — do not flag "Train 6 days each week." Approved ceremonial numerals may be serif.)
- Instrument Serif used for body, data, or more than one signature phrase → **reject.**

**Geometry**
- Radius > 2 on anything operational; buttons not square; `surface`(14) radius used off device-chrome; pill(999) off mono chips → **reject.**
- Athlete-facing tap target < 44px; set-log action < 64px → **reject.**

**Color / gold / literals**
- A repeated semantic color/type/radius/motion/touch value in feature code instead of the canonical token layer → **reject.** Responsive composition may use local layout values when they do not create a competing design role; document genuine one-offs.
- Styling that breaks `[data-theme="light"]`, or a **dark-native asset filtered into light** → **reject.** Light uses light-native anatomy (or stays typographic when none exists).
- Gold as decoration: confetti, gloss/gradient "premium," glow on operational CTAs, unearned emphasis → **reject.** Gold marks real state/structure or goes.

**Sign in with Apple**
- Any redrawn, approximated, substituted, or restyled Apple mark / custom SVG apple glyph → **reject.** Use Apple's official Sign in with Apple control (web JS button / `ASAuthorizationAppleIDButton`).

**Voice**
- Hype, begging, flattery, over-explaining, unprovable claims → **reject.**
- No real signal → emit **empty string**, not counterfeit care.
- Periodization jargon / coaching essays on chrome → **reject.** Chrome = facts, one fact one place.

**Account / Receipt surfaces** (`train/**`, account panels) — representation only
- Any status (`Last synced`, import "complete") shown without a confirmed server round-trip this session → **reject.** Server-confirmed or silent (`Not confirmed` / omit).
- Premium framing on missing entitlement (Upgrade / Unlock / lock glyph / blurred preview) → **reject.** Absence is a fact: `Not on this account`.
- Copy implying access loss = record loss → **reject.**
- Describing email (incl. Apple relay) as the identity, or prompting the athlete to authorize a merge → **reject.** (DB keying is the schema ruling's job — don't invent it here either.)
- Auth bundled with marketing consent → **reject.** Launch email is a separate optional checkbox.
- Treating client `ACCESS_MODE` as security → **reject.** Real gate = server-backed entitlements.

**Portal Focus mode** (temporary web contract)
- Auto-completing a session, hiding prescribed values, dropping `/ side`, adding a rest timer, or moving cues out from behind `?` → **reject.** Do not project this web contract onto native mode truth without its own ruling.

